    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a start, but it feels a little generic. When we talk about \"urban-friendly,\" we're really looking to speak the language of the community to avoid looking like a corporate giant that doesn't understand the culture. Could you take it a step further? Try drafting a version that uses more authentic slang or a more rhythmic, street-style dialect that would really land with people in those areas. We want it to feel like it's coming from someone who actually knows the vibe of the neighborhood.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
